  message: "Owner decision 2026-11-10: PARKED. Local narrowing stays opt-in; the goal of making it the default is dropped. Reasons, measured (details on WI-zajuv): with the WI-zunug fix (a), narrowing applies to about 18 percent of commits that touch package source (20 of 113; the rest change import-time code, where every importer must run); and 69 test files read the whole tree as text, about 50 of which match any one source file, a floor of roughly 3 minutes wall on 6 CPUs for any selector narrower than the import graph. Not reopened unless the whole-tree reader set gets built (option 1 on WI-zajuv: reads markers, verified per test). Alternatives filed: WI-fipuf (failure-first ordering), WI-nupit (four slow whole-tree tests). Applies here because a per-function static selector is also narrower than the import graph and would drop the same whole-tree readers."  # 8cdf
